<h2>Phase 1 — Financing</h2>

<div class="step auto"><div class="num">1</div><div>
<h4>Send the Cherry link <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Send the customer the Cherry application link: <code>https://pay.withcherry.com/hearing-benefit-services</code></p>
<p>Then add the tag <code>cherry_link_sent</code> to the contact. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> GHL creates the opportunity at <strong>Financing Link Sent</strong>.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">2</div><div>
<h4>Check the Cherry portal daily <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Cherry does not update GHL by itself. Check the Cherry merchant portal at least once per business day for every open card in stages 1–8.</p>
<ul>
<li>Customer started the application → drag card to <strong>Application Started</strong></li>
<li>Approved → add tag <code>cherry_approved</code></li>
<li>Declined or partially approved → add tag <code>cherry_declined</code>, then contact the customer about options</li>
</ul>
</div></div>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">3</div><div>
<h4>Send the payment plan <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Send the payment plan from the Cherry portal and drag the card to <strong>Payment Plan Sent</strong>.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">4</div><div>
<h4>Send the Patient Agreement <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Send the Patient Agreement, then add the tag <code>cherry_agreement_sent</code>. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> The card moves to <strong>Patient Agreement Sent</strong>.</p>
<p>When the agreement is signed and the down payment is made, drag the card to <strong>Agreement Signed — Down Payment Made</strong>.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">5</div><div>
<h4>Confirm funding <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>When the Cherry portal shows funds paid to HBS, add the tag <code>cherry_funded</code>. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> The card moves to <strong>Funds Received by HBS</strong> and your Signia ordering task is created.</p>
</div></div>

<h2>Phase 2 — Fulfillment</h2>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">6</div><div>
<h4>Order on the Signia shop <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Task: <em>Order hearing aids on Signia shop</em> (due next day, 4:00 PM).</p>
<p>Place the order on the Signia shop, then drag the card to <strong>Ordered on Signia Shop</strong>. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> The Hearing Professional gets an "Incoming Signia device" task.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step hp"><div class="num">7</div><div>
<h4>Receive and program the device <span class="pill p-hp">HEARING PROFESSIONAL</span></h4>
<p>When the device arrives, drag the card to <strong>Received by Andrea</strong>.</p>
<p>After programming, drag it to <strong>Programming Complete</strong>. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> The Order Coordinator gets the shipping-label task. You no longer need to message anyone; moving the card is the notification.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">8</div><div>
<h4>Create the label and send it <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Create the UPS label in PirateShip, then drag the card to <strong>PirateShip Label Created</strong>.</p>
<p>Send the label to the Hearing Professional on WhatsApp, then drag the card to <strong>Label Sent to Andrea (WhatsApp)</strong>. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> The UPS drop-off task is created.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step hp"><div class="num">9</div><div>
<h4>Drop off at UPS <span class="pill p-hp">HEARING PROFESSIONAL</span></h4>
<p>Drop the package at UPS, then drag the card to <strong>Dropped Off at UPS — In Transit</strong>. <span class="pill p-auto">AUTOMATED</span> The Order Coordinator gets a delivery-check task due in 3 days.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="step oc"><div class="num">10</div><div>
<h4>Confirm delivery and check in <span class="pill p-oc">ORDER COORDINATOR</span></h4>
<p>Check the UPS tracking. When it shows delivered, drag the card to <strong>Delivered</strong>.</p>
<p>Two days later, contact the customer to make sure everything is working, then drag the card to <strong>Day 2 Check-In</strong>.</p>
</div></div>

<h2>Tags Reference</h2>
<div class="tbl"><table>
<tr><th>Tag</th><th>When to add it</th><th>What happens</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_link_sent</code></td><td>After sending the Cherry link</td><td>Opportunity created at Financing Link Sent</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_approved</code></td><td>Portal shows approval</td><td>Card moves to Approved — Awaiting Plan Selection</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_declined</code></td><td>Portal shows decline or partial approval</td><td>Card moves to Declined / Partial Approval</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_agreement_sent</code></td><td>After sending the Patient Agreement</td><td>Card moves to Patient Agreement Sent</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_funded</code></td><td>Portal shows funds paid to HBS</td><td>Card moves to Funds Received + Signia order task</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_shipped</code></td><td>Optional; dragging the card does the same</td><td>Card moves to Dropped Off at UPS — In Transit</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cherry_stalled</code></td><td>Customer stops responding</td><td>Card moves to Stalled — No Response</td></tr>
</table></div>

<div class="warn"><strong>Use the right tag.</strong> Older tags with similar names already exist (<code>cherry pre-approved</code>, <code>cherry-approved-high</code>, <code>cherry-approved-mid</code>, <code>cherry-approved-low</code>). They do <strong>not</strong> move cards. Always use the underscore versions listed above.</div>

<h2>Things to Know</h2>
<div class="card">
<ul>
<li><strong>Cards only move forward by tag.</strong> If a card needs to go back (for example, approved and then declined), drag it by hand.</li>
<li><strong>One open card per customer.</strong> If a customer already has an open card in this pipeline, adding <code>cherry_link_sent</code> again will not create a second one.</li>
<li><strong>Closed Lost / Refund:</strong> drag the card by hand and add a note explaining why.</li>
<li><strong>Tasks:</strong> check your GHL task list every morning. Each task tells you exactly which stage to move the card to when you're done.</li>
</ul>
</div>

